-- title:
--   Near each period the repeated template is a single shifted copy
-- statement:
--   A velocity $v$ has time collars when $v(t,\cdot)=0$ for $t<\frac14$ and for $t>\frac34$. Its repetition is the $1$-periodic field $\tilde v(t,x)=\sum_{n\in\mathbb Z}v(t-n,x)$. If $v$ has time collars, $n\in\mathbb Z$ and $-\frac14<t-n<\frac54$, then
--   $$
--   \tilde v(t,x)=v(t-n,x)\qquad(x\in\mathbb R^3).
--   $$
--
--   So, locally in time, the periodic repetition looks like one copy of the template.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/MathematicalPhysics/NavierStokes/BalancedTransport/Periodic.lean#L17-L32

